<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali ibn Hatim</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali ibn Hatim was the last ruler of the Hamdanid sultanate of Sanaa, an Isma'ili tribal dynasty of 12th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. When the Ayyubid prince Turan-Shah invaded Yemen in 1174, he fled to the mountains, and by the 1180s Sanaa had passed to Ayyubid rule, ending Isma'ili political power in Yemen.</p></div>
